course: dictionary
lesson: 4149
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Glue can be a thing or an action. «Super glue sticks skin together in seconds, so only an adult uses it.» Here glue is the sticky stuff in the tube.
explain: Glue can also be an action word. «Glue the wings onto the model plane» means stick them on with glue. Ask yourself what someone is doing: if they are doing something, the word is probably a verb.
explain: Glue has a third meaning in the phrase «glued to». «Ella was glued to the screen all afternoon» does not mean she was stuck with glue. It means she could not stop watching. Put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Glue is a sticky substance used to join things together.
fact: To glue something means to stick it with glue.
fact: «Glued to» something means not able to stop looking at it or staying close to it.
fact: Super glue is very strong, so children use it only with an adult.
fact: «Caddis fly larvae glue sand grains and tiny shells together with silk» to make a protective case.
exercise: «Caddis fly larvae glue sand grains and tiny shells together with silk.» What does glue mean here? | To paint something bright | To melt something down | To cut something into pieces | *To stick something with glue
exercise: «Ella was glued to the screen all afternoon.» What does glued to mean? | *Could not stop watching it | Got bored quickly | Stuck to the screen with glue | Sat very close to a window
exercise: «Pass me the glue, please.» What is glue in this sentence? | *A sticky substance used to join things | A piece of card | A pair of scissors | A pencil case
test: «Glue the wings onto the model plane.» In this sentence, what kind of word is glue? | A question word | An adjective, describing a word | A noun, a thing | *A verb, an action
test: What does «glued to the TV» mean? | Standing very close by | Stuck to the TV with glue | Turned off and put away | *Watching it without stopping
exam: In «Hold the pieces together while the glue dries», what does glue mean? | *A sticky substance used to join things | A type of paper used for drawing | To cut something into small pieces | To stop looking at something
